      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The historic Libertyville Civic Center, built in 1935 as a post office, now houses the village library and community events.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.visitlakecounty.org/libertyville",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The village library began in the Cook Mansion, donated by Emily Cook in 1920, and later moved to the remodeled 1921 building with a Colonial facade.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3,
        16,
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Libertyville%2C_Illinois",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Mickey Finn’s Brewery, opened in 1994 on Main Street, is a landmark for handcrafted beer and social gatherings.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.visitlakecounty.org/libertyville",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Libertyville lies just five miles west of Lake Michigan, bordered by Gages Lake and Gurnee to the north and Vernon Hills to the south.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21,
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Libertyville%2C_Illinois",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "location_description"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "The village was named after settler George Vardin, who moved there in 1835, and the post office adopted the name Libertyville in 1837.",
